%C CAN control utility

Syntax:
    canctrl (interface) [options]
Options:
    devinfo         get device info. If no option is specified
                    this is the default

    timing          get nominal bittiming options for (interface)
    timing[:topts]  set nominal bittiming options for (interface)
    dtiming         get data bittiming options for (interface)
    dtiming[:topts] set data bittiming options for (interface)

    maxtxq          get maxtxq for (interface)
    maxtxq=<num>    set maxtxq for (interface)
    maxrxq          get maxrxq for (interface)
    maxrxq=<num>    set maxrxq for (interface)

    chnlopt         get channel options for (interface)
    chnlopt[:copts] set channel options for (interface)

    up              set (interface) to IFUP state
    down            set (interface) to IFDOWN state


Incomplete/Testing Options:
    filter      set filter for (interface)
    sockopt     set sockopt for (interface)
    chnlopt     set channel options for (interface)

topts - Timing specific options
A comma separated list of key=value pairs. Valid keys are:
    bitrate      - Bitrate in bps
    clkrate      - Input clock in Hz
    sample_point - Sample point in tenths of a percent
    tq           - Tq value in ns
    prop_seg     - # of Tqs in propegation segment
    phase_seg1   - # of Tqs in phase1 segment
    phase_seg2   - # of Tqs in phase2 segment
    sjw          - # of Tqs
    brp          - Presale (divide) clkrate
Not all interfaces support every possible topt.

copts - Channel specific options
A comma separated list of key=value pairs. Valid keys are:
    fd=[1|0]       - Enable/disable fd
    listen=[1|0]   - Enable/disable listen only (Tx is disabled)
    loopback=[1|0] - Enable/disable loopback mode
    self_ack=[1|0] - Enable/disable sending an ACK when transmitting
    extended=[1|0] - Enable/disable extended IDs

Examples:
/* set p_ch0 down */
    canctrl p_ch0 down

/* set custom timing (interface must be down) */
    canctrl p_ch0 timing:bitrate=250000,clkrate=24,sample_point=85,tq=1,prop_seg=0,phase_seg1=12,phase_seg2=1,sjw=1,brp=5

/* set loopback and extended MID for channel 2 */
    canctrl p_ch2 chnlopt:loopback=1,extended=1
